## Testing\
\
### Backend (pytest)\
\
Test every endpoint returns the right shape. Test the upsert rule explicitly \'97 insert a row with views=500, then upsert with views=0, and assert views is still 500.\
\
### Frontend (if playwright \'97 headless, always; ask your user what test patterns they want to use, mcp servers are also an option, or connected chrome extensions)\
\
Verify the page loads (not blank = not crashed), key sections render, sort works, filter pills work.\
\
**Force headless in your config:**\
```ts\
// playwright.config.ts\
export default defineConfig(\{\
  use: \{ headless: true \},\
\});\
```\
\
AI assistants often try to launch headed browsers from background agents. This pops Chrome windows on your desktop, steals focus, and can trigger security flags on platforms you're scraping. Always headless. No exceptions.\
\
### After every code change\
\
1. **Python changed** \uc0\u8594  restart the backend. Don't ask, just do it. Then verify multiple endpoints (not just `/health` \'97 a server can return healthy while every other route 500s).\
2. **Frontend changed** \uc0\u8594  take a headless screenshot. Verify the page loads and the changed section renders. Blank page = React crash.\
3. Run the test suite.\
4. Commit with a short descriptive message.\
\
